This is a modified fork of Liam ERD, pinned to upstream commit 92156eac5
(2026-06-18). Files that differ from that commit carry a notice at the top of
the file, as required by section 4(b) of the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Summary of the changes made to the original work
------------------------------------------------

1. Table positions are persisted.
   Upstream recomputes the automatic layout on every load, so any table the
   user dragged snapped back on refresh. Positions now resolve as
   URL (?positions=) > browser storage > layout.json > automatic layout, and a
   table that is not pinned still falls back to the automatic layout.

2. Canvas memos.
   Free-form notes can be pinned to the diagram, shipped with the build in
   memos.json and edited in the browser.

3. Colour coding.
   Tables and memos can be tinted from a fixed palette taken from the existing
   design tokens. A table's colour is stored alongside its position.

4. A read-only default with an explicit edit mode.
   Everything above is read-only unless the page is opened with ?edit=1, so a
   shared link cannot be rearranged by accident.

5. MySQL schema export.
   Upstream can deparse a schema to PostgreSQL and YAML only. A MySQL deparser
   was added, and the export menu can now copy the DDL to the clipboard or
   download it as a .sql file.

6. A Windows compatibility fix to an npm script in frontend/apps/app, which
   otherwise prevented the repository's own lint task from running.
